{
  "_note": "Genre profiles: default weights for tags. A list's weight in a story is the biggest weight among its tags; a list whose tags the mix does not mention gets only the wildcard floor. Picking 'western' and 'fairy tale' blends those two profiles equally. A genre name not listed here still works: it becomes a tag with weight 3. Add your own in ~/.storywheel/genres.json.",
  "_floor": 0.12,
  "_neighbors_note": "The wildcard floor draws mostly from untagged lists and from lists tagged with a neighbor of the story's genres; other genres get only a tenth of it between them.",
  "_floors_note": "The floor is the share of picks that go to lists the mix does not mention. 0.12 suits one-off blocks (a disaster, a stranger). Slots that repeat all through a story (rival, job, place, names, landmark) get a lower one here, so an off-genre rival does not show up in half the sentences.",
